  "prefLabel": "Plc 2106.01 Non-binding Arbitration Preliminary Procedures",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 2106.01 Non-binding Arbitration Preliminary Procedures.\n\n(a) If the parties select non-binding arbitration, the OPLC shall provide the parties with résumés of 3 individuals who meet the qualifications specified in Plc 2103.03(b).\n\n(b) Within 10 days of receiving the résumés, the parties shall select an arbitrator using the criteria in Plc 2103.03(d), and may select an alternate arbitrator in the event the chosen arbitrator becomes unavailable.\n\n(c) If the arbitrator withdraws, has a conflict of interest, or is otherwise unavailable, and the parties did not preselect an alternate, the OPLC shall appoint an arbitrator who meets the criteria in Plc 2103.03(d) to engage with the parties.\n\nSource. #14331, eff 8-20-25, EXPIRES: 8-20-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc2100.html"
